TI  - Comprehensive Proteomics Metadata and Integrative Web Portals Facilitate Sharing 
      and Integration of LINCS Multiomics Data.
PG  - 100947
LID - S1535-9476(25)00045-3 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.mcpro.2025.100947 [doi]
LID - 100947
AB  - The Library of Integrated Network-based Cellular Signatures (LINCS), an NIH 
      Common Fund program, has cataloged and analyzed cellular function and molecular 
      activity profiles in response to >80,000 perturbing agents that are potentially 
      disruptive to cells. Because of the importance of proteins and their 
      modifications to the response of specific cellular perturbations, four of the six 
      LINCS centers have included significant proteomics efforts in the 
      characterization of the resulting phenotype. This manuscript aims to describe 
      this effort and the data harmonization and integration of the LINCS proteomics 
      data discussed in recent LINCS papers.
